From 9b326f5da44a51077c7a82e3798f5635603aea51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:24:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] l2r-local: entry 23-o: the glue defers boxes with a
 wide header through defer_wide

The lowering of `reussir.rc.defer` calls __reussir_drop_defer_wide (23-n)
for a box whose first 8 bytes are header with 16 spare bits, so that the
stack links the pending boxes through their headers instead of keeping an
entry or a cell each:
- a fused variant box: the 32-bit count, then the i32 tag; the tag is
  below 2^16 when the variant has at most 2^16 arms;
- a compound record box whose payload starts at offset 8 or later: the
  count, then padding (the box is `{i32, payload}`, not packed, so the
  payload starts at its alignment; a packed record's is 1).
Other boxes (a compound record aligned to 4 or less, as on 32-bit
targets without 8-byte members) keep __reussir_drop_defer. The release
functions read neither the count nor the bits above the tag, and the
runtime writes both back before a release runs.

Every Worklist variant qualifies, and on 64-bit targets every Worklist
compound record (its box members are 8-byte pointers). lean2rr's
RtAltTreeFree, whose levels each leave a node of the other type pending,
took 24 bytes per pending node (runs of one, the release functions
alternating); now none.

Tests: conversion/drop_stack_ops.mlir (a compound record aligned to 8 and
a variant through the wide entry, one aligned to 4 through the plain
one); frontend/worklist_drop_depth.rr gains a chain of two mutually
recursive types whose levels each leave a small node of the other type
pending, 10^6 levels on a 256 KiB stack: peak RSS must grow by less than
16 MiB (it grew by 45060 KiB with 23-a to 23-m only), and the ASan run
of sanitizer/e2e/worklist_drop_depth.rr frees it at 10^5 levels;
codegen/retcon_drop_targets.rr, executable_pic_default_retcon.rr and
frontend/retcon_drop.rr expect the wide entry for their recursive enums.
